    "text_delta": "roadcaster, know whether this panel composition broke procedural rules, and can advise on whether other candidates have raised similar concerns.\n\n#### Step 4: Decide how to frame the issue\n* **If raising it informally:** During your feedback discussion, you can ask neutrally:  \n  > *\"I noticed the panel was entirely male. Does the broadcaster have a policy regarding panel diversity for senior editorial appointments?\"*  \n  This signals that you noticed the irregularity without immediately lodging an adversarial accusation.\n* **If raising it formally:** If the written feedback seems flimsy, your qualifications clearly outweighed the successful candidate's, and the broadcaster violated panel-composition rules, you may consider a formal internal grievance or consulting an employment lawyer specializing in discrimination.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\nAn all-male panel for a senior news role in public media is a red flag regarding governance and culture, but it is best used as supporting context rather than your standalone argument. Start by securing written feedback, checking their recruitment policies, and consulting a staff or union representative.\n",
